Chapter: BoundedBudgetedAccepted
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Cost Model, the budgeted rung, the arm that must COMPILE.
 `codex/test/errors/bounded-budgeted-exceeded` proves the refusal; a refusal
 arm alone cannot tell a working check from one that refuses everything, so
 this is the control.

 Both shapes the rung was ruled into existence for (CurrentPlan 17 and 18):
 `field` slices a FIXED WIDTH out of a line of any length, which is bounded by
 the literal it passes and not by the line; `digits` converts an Integer,
 which is bounded by a constant nobody states. Neither is `fixed` -- the bytes
 are not the same every call -- and calling either `linear` would have been a
 promise about the input that is not true.

Section: A Bound The Caller Names

  bounded budgeted field : Text -> Text
  field (line) = substring line 0 4

Section: A Bound Nobody States

  bounded budgeted digits : Integer -> Text
  digits (n) = integer-to-text n

Section: The Predicates Allocate Nothing

 Measured 2026-08-19 at 0 bytes on 64 and 256 characters, so they are `none`
 in the registry and a budgeted ceiling holds over them trivially.

 THE TWO PREDICATES ARE STILL SEPARATE FUNCTIONS RATHER THAN ONE JOINED BY
 `&`, and the reason is no longer a defect. When this arm was written a
 boolean `&` was refused CDX6101 under `bounded none`, because `infer-and`
 recorded the expression type on its Text arm and not its boolean one; that
 was fixed the same day and `bounded-none-accepted` now carries all three
 boolean shapes as its regression guard. They stay apart here so this arm
 tests the budgeted rung and nothing else.

  bounded budgeted looks : Text -> Boolean
  looks (s) = text-contains s "x"

  bounded budgeted starts : Text -> Boolean
  starts (s) = text-starts-with s "y"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("field=" & field "abcdefghij")
    print-line-uni ("digits=" & digits 4096)
    print-line-uni ("looks=" & (if looks "yxz" then "True" else "False"))
    print-line-uni ("starts=" & (if starts "yxz" then "True" else "False"))
  end
